resource:Air dc11:description "The element of air, along with fire, earth, and water, is one of the four traditional elements in cosmogonies in both Western and Eastern traditions. It is present in all religions and their rituals, in esoteric philosophy, in alchemy, and in astrology. It is considered 'active and masculine,' just like the element of fire, in contrast to earth and water, which are considered 'passive and feminine."@en;
             a sosa:FeatureOfInterest,
               owl:NamedIndividual;
             rdfs:comment "Air"@en.
resource:Atmosphere_of_Earth dc11:description "The Earth's atmosphere is the gaseous part of the Earth, making it the outermost and least dense layer of the planet. It consists of various gases that vary in quantity depending on altitude. This mixture of gases that forms the atmosphere is commonly referred to as air. Approximately 75% of the atmospheric mass is located within the first 11 kilometers from the sea surface. The primary gases that make up the atmosphere are oxygen (21%) and nitrogen (78%), followed by argon, carbon dioxide, and water vapor."@en;
                             a sosa:FeatureOfInterest,
                               owl:NamedIndividual.
resource:Chlorophyll dc11:description "Chlorophylls (from the Greek words χλωρος, chloros, meaning 'green,' and φύλλον, fýlon, meaning 'leaf') are a family of green-colored pigments found in cyanobacteria and in all organisms that possess chloroplasts or thylakoid membranes in their cells, which includes plants and various types of algae. Chlorophyll is a highly essential biomolecule, critical in the process of photosynthesis, which enables plants and algae to store energy from sunlight."@en;
                     a vas:Vegetation_Property,
                       owl:NamedIndividual;
                     rdfs:label "Chl"@en;
                     sosa:isObservedBy vas:OTCI_S3_Sensor_1,
                                       vas:Chl_g_Sensor_1,
                                       vas:Chl_S2_Sensor_1,
                                       vas:Chl_L9_Sensor_1,
                                       vas:Chl_L8_Sensor_1.
resource:Diffuse_sky_radiation a vas:Radiation_Property,
                                 owl:NamedIndividual;
                               rdfs:comment "Diffuse irradiation is the one that reaches the earth's surface from the sky except for the sun due to the scattering and reflection by the compositions of the atmosphere."@en;
                               rdfs:label "diffuse_irradiance"@en;
                               sosa:isObservedBy vas:I_dif_g_RAD_Sensor_1.
resource:Direct_insolation a vas:Radiation_Property,
                             owl:NamedIndividual;
                           rdfs:comment "Direct radiation is the solar radiation which travels on a straight line from the sun down to the earth׳s surface"@en;
                           rdfs:label "direct_irradiance_at_the_surface"@en;
                           sosa:isObservedBy vas:I_dir_g_RAD_Sensor_1.
resource:Drought dc11:description "Drought is a transient climatological anomaly in which the availability of water falls below the usual levels in a geographical area. There is not enough water to meet the needs of plants, animals, and humans residing in that area. The primary cause of all droughts is a lack of rain or precipitation, known as meteorological drought. If it persists, it can lead to a condition characterized by an imbalance between the natural water supply and the natural water demand. In extreme cases, it can lead to aridity."@es;
                 a resource:Soil_Property,
                   owl:NamedIndividual;
                 rdfs:label "Drought"@en;
                 sosa:isObservedBy vas:DroughtIndex_SMOS_CATDS_Sensor_1.
resource:Enhanced_vegetation_index a owl:NamedIndividual,
                                     vas:Vegetation_Property;
                                   rdfs:comment "The enhanced vegetation index (EVI) is an 'optimized' vegetation index designed to enhance the vegetation signal with improved sensitivity in high biomass regions and improved vegetation monitoring through a de-coupling of the canopy background signal and a reduction in atmosphere influences. EVI is computed following this equation: where: * NIR/red/blue are atmospherically-corrected and partially atmosphere corrected (Rayleigh and ozone absorption) surface reflectances * L is the canopy background adjustment that addresses non-linear, differential NIR and red radiant transfer through a canopy, and * C1, C2 are the coefficients of the aerosol resistance term, which uses the blue band to correct for aerosol influences in the red band. The coefficients adopted in the MODIS-EVI algorithm are: L=1, C1 = 6, C2 = 7.5, and G (gain factor) = 2.5. Whereas the Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI) is chlorophyll sensitive, the EVI is more responsive to canopy structural variations, including leaf area index (LAI), canopy type, plant physiognomy, and canopy architecture. The two vegetation indices complement each other in global vegetation studies and improve upon the detection of vegetation changes and extraction of canopy biophysical parameters.. Another difference between Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI) and EVI is that in the presence of snow, NDVI decreases, while EVI increases (Huete, 2002). Starting 2000, and after the launch of the two MODIS sensors on Terra (satellite) and Aqua (satellite) by NASA, EVI was adopted as a standard product by NASA and became extremely popular with users due to its ability to eliminate background and atmosphere noises, as well as its non saturation, a typical NDVI problem. EVI is currently distributed for free by the USGS LP DAAC. (en)"@en;
                                   rdfs:label "EVI"@en;
                                   sosa:isObservedBy vas:EVI_UAV_Multispectral_Sensor_1,
                                                     vas:EVI_L9_Sensor_1,
                                                     vas:EVI_L8_Sensor_1,
                                                     vas:EVI_diary_500m_t_Sensor_1,
                                                     vas:EVI_S2_Sensor_1,
                                                     vas:EVI_diary_500m_a_Sensor_1.
resource:Humidity dc11:description "The humidity of the air is due to the water vapor present in the atmosphere. This vapor comes from the evaporation of terrestrial water bodies. The amount of water vapor that air can hold depends on its temperature. Warm air can hold more water vapor than cold air. One way to measure atmospheric humidity is through a hygrometer"@en;
                  a resource:Meteorology_Property,
                    owl:NamedIndividual.
resource:Land_surface dc11:description "Earth's relief refers to the term that defines the shapes and features of the Earth's crust or lithosphere on the surface, both concerning landforms on emerged lands and the oceanic relief, which pertains to the seafloor. It is the subject of study in geomorphology and physical geography, especially when referring to continental and island lands. Pierre George provides a simple definition of Earth's relief: The Earth's relief is the raised part of the globe's surface, such as hills or mountains."@en;
                      a sosa:FeatureOfInterest,
                        owl:NamedIndividual.
resource:Meteorology_Property a owl:Class;
                              rdfs:comment "Class that represents all Meteorological properties"@en;
                              rdfs:subClassOf sosa:ObservableProperty.
resource:Orthophoto a vas:Vegetation_Property,
                      resource:Soil_Property,
                      owl:NamedIndividual;
                    rdfs:comment "geometrically corrected aerial photograph"@en;
                    sosa:isObservedBy vas:Orthophoto_UAV_RGB_Sensor_1.
resource:Plant_disease a vas:Vegetation_Property,
                         owl:NamedIndividual;
                       rdfs:comment "Spectral indicator of plant disease or pathogen-induced stress."@en;
                       rdfs:label "DiseaseStatus";
                       sosa:isObservedBy vas:DiseaseStatus_UAV_Hyperspectral_Sensor_1.
resource:Radiation dc11:description "The phenomenon of radiation is the propagation of energy in the form of electromagnetic waves or subatomic particles through a vacuum or a material medium. There are different forms of radiation with distinct properties and effects."@en;
                   a sosa:FeatureOfInterest,
                     owl:NamedIndividual.
resource:Soil dc11:description "The term 'soil' refers to the surface layer of the Earth's crust that is biologically active and originates from the physical or chemical disintegration or alteration of rocks, as well as from the residues of living organisms that settle upon it. Many processes can contribute to the formation of a specific type of soil, including aeolian deposition, sedimentation in watercourses, weathering, and the deposition of organic material"@en;
              a sosa:FeatureOfInterest,
                owl:NamedIndividual.
resource:Soil-adjusted_vegetation_index a vas:Vegetation_Property,
                                          owl:NamedIndividual;
                                        rdfs:comment "Empirically derived NDVI products have been shown to be unstable, varying with soil colour, soil moisture, and saturation effects from high density vegetation. In an attempt to improve NDVI, Huete developed a vegetation index that accounted for the differential red and near-infrared extinction through the vegetation canopy. The index is a transformation technique that minimizes soil brightness influences from spectral vegetation indices involving red and near-infrared (NIR) wavelengths. The index is given as: where L is a canopy background adjustment factor. An L value of 0.5 in reflectance space was found to minimize soil brightness variations and eliminate the need for additional calibration for different soils.The transformation was found to nearly eliminate soil-induced variations in vegetation indices. (en)"@en;
                                        rdfs:label "SAVI"@en;
                                        sosa:isObservedBy vas:SAVI_UAV_Multispectral_Sensor_1,
                                                          vas:SAVI_S2_Sensor_1,
                                                          vas:SAVI_L9_Sensor_1,
                                                          vas:SAVI_L8_Sensor_1.
resource:Soil_Property a owl:Class;
                       rdfs:comment "Class that represents all Soil properties"@en;
                       rdfs:subClassOf sosa:ObservableProperty.
resource:Soil_moisture a owl:NamedIndividual,
                         resource:Soil_Property;
                       rdfs:comment "Soil moisture is the water content of the soil. It can be expressed in terms of volume or weight. Soil moisture measurement can be based on in situ probes (e.g., capacitance probes, neutron probes) or remote sensing methods. Water that enters a field is removed from a field by runoff, drainage, evaporation or transpiration."@en;
                       rdfs:label "SM"@en;
                       sosa:isObservedBy vas:SM_g_Sensor_4,
                                         vas:SM_NRT_SMOS_ESA_Sensor_1,
                                         vas:SM_SMOS_BEC_Sensor_1,
                                         vas:SM_UAV_Microwave_Sensor_1,
                                         vas:SM_SMAP-S1_9km_Sensor_1,
                                         vas:SM_g_Sensor_6,
                                         vas:SM_SMAP-S1_3km_Sensor_1,
                                         vas:SM_SMOS-IC_CATDS_Sensor_1,
                                         vas:SM_g_Sensor_3,
                                         vas:SM_S1_Sensor_1,
                                         vas:SM_g_Sensor_1,
                                         vas:SM_g_Sensor_2,
                                         vas:SM_g_Sensor_5,
                                         vas:SM_SMOS_ESA_Sensor_1,
                                         vas:SM_SMAP_36km_Sensor_1,
                                         vas:SM_freeze_and_Thaw_SMOS_ESA_Sensor_1.
resource:Vegetation dc11:description "Vegetation refers to the coverage of wild or cultivated plants (flora) that grow spontaneously in a geographic area, whether on the land surface or in an aquatic environment. It is also referred to as vegetation cover. Its distribution on Earth depends on climatic factors and soils. Vegetation is so important that climate types are even categorized based on the type of vegetation that grows in the areas where they dominate. This is why we talk about a jungle climate, a savanna climate, a taiga climate, among other rainy climates, etc."@en;
                    a sosa:FeatureOfInterest,
                      owl:NamedIndividual.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#baresoilpercentage> a owl:FunctionalProperty,
                                                                         owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                                       rdfs:comment """Bare soil percentage

Example: 35.747452"""@en;
                                                                       rdfs:domain vas:Sentinel-2_Product;
                                                                       rdfs:label "Bare soil percentage"@en;
                                                                       rdfs:range xsd:decimal;
                                                                       rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:sentinel2ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#cloudcover> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                               rdfs:comment """Cloud coverage (percent) of a WRS scene.

Values:
0.00 - 100.00
-1 = Cloud cover not calculated or assessed"""@en;
                                                               rdfs:domain vas:Landsat-8_Product;
                                                               rdfs:label "Cloud cover"@en;
                                                               rdfs:range xsd:decimal;
                                                               rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:landsat8ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#cloudcoverland> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                                   rdfs:comment """All sensors = Cloud coverage over land (percent) assigned to a WRS scene.

Values:
-1 = Cloud cover land not calculated or assessed."""@en;
                                                                   rdfs:domain vas:Landsat-8_Product;
                                                                   rdfs:label "Cloud cover land"@en;
                                                                   rdfs:range xsd:decimal;
                                                                   rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:landsat8ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#collectioncategory> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                                       rdfs:comment """Landsat Collection 1 is organized by a tiered inventory structure to indicate the quality and level of processing of the data.

Values:
T1 = Tier 1 is the highest available quality and processing level. This category is suitable for time-series analysis across the different Landsat sensors.

T2 = Tier 2 scenes contain significant cloud cover and have insufficient ground control to generate precision and terrain corrected products.

RT = Real-Time indicates initial processing with additional processing required to achieve Tier 1 or Tier 2."""@en;
                                                                       rdfs:domain vas:Landsat-8_Product;
                                                                       rdfs:label "Collection category"@en;
                                                                       rdfs:range xsd:string;
                                                                       rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:landsat8ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#dateacquired> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                                 rdfs:comment """Year, month and day that this scene was imaged.

Format:
YYYY/MM/DD"""@en;
                                                                 rdfs:domain vas:Landsat-8_Product;
                                                                 rdfs:label "Date acquired"@en;
                                                                 rdfs:range xsd:dateTime;
                                                                 rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:landsat8ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#datum> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                          rdfs:comment """Datum used in creating the image.

Values:
WGS84 = World Geodetic System 1984"""@en;
                                                          rdfs:domain vas:Landsat-8_Product;
                                                          rdfs:label "Datum"@en;
                                                          rdfs:range xsd:string;
                                                          rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:landsat8ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#filename> a owl:FunctionalProperty,
                                                               owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                             rdfs:comment """Package file name, with extension ‘.SAFE’.

Example: S2B_MSIL2A_20180628T105619_N0208_R094_T30SUF_20180628T151421.SAFE"""@en;
                                                             rdfs:domain vas:Sentinel-3_Product,
                                                                         vas:Sentinel-2_Product,
                                                                         vas:SMOS_Product;
                                                             rdfs:label "Filename"@en;
                                                             rdfs:range xsd:string;
                                                             rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:commonProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#footprint> a owl:FunctionalProperty,
                                                                owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                              rdfs:comment """Boundaries of the frame in a simplified form.The coordinates shall be declared in a counter-clockwise order.

Example: 
POLYGON ((-5.248379903953922 37.02527578563511,-4.014302538465313 37.042247242200354,-4.001451962964202 36.05254100905861,-5.219917191699283 36.03616769808406,-5.248379903953922 37.02527578563511))"""@en;
                                                              rdfs:domain vas:Sentinel-3_Product,
                                                                          vas:Sentinel-2_Product,
                                                                          vas:Landsat-8_Product;
                                                              rdfs:label "Footprint"@en;
                                                              rdfs:range geosparql:wktLiteral;
                                                              rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:commonProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#highprobacloudspercentage> a owl:FunctionalProperty,
                                                                                owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                                              rdfs:comment """High proba clouds percentage

Example: 0.232073"""@en;
                                                                              rdfs:domain vas:Sentinel-2_Product;
                                                                              rdfs:label "High proba clouds percentage"@en;
                                                                              rdfs:range xsd:decimal;
                                                                              rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:sentinel2ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#identifier> a owl:FunctionalProperty,
                                                                 owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                               rdfs:comment """Identifier

Example: S2A_MSIL1C_20180603T110041_N0206_R094_T30SUF_20180603T130559"""@en;
                                                               rdfs:domain vas:Sentinel-2_Product;
                                                               rdfs:label "Identifier"@en;
                                                               rdfs:range xsd:string;
                                                               rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:sentinel2ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#imagequalityoli> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                                    rdfs:comment """Composite image quality for the bands. For Landsat 8 or 9, if scene is OLI or OLI_TIRS combined, value will reflect OLI quality score. If TIRS, the TIRS quality score will be used

Values:
9 = Best
0 = Worst
-1 = Image quality not calculated or assessed"""@en;
                                                                    rdfs:domain vas:Landsat-8_Product;
                                                                    rdfs:label "Image quality OLI"@en;
                                                                    rdfs:range xsd:decimal;
                                                                    rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:landsat8ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#imagequalitytirs> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                                     rdfs:comment """Composite image quality for the bands. For Landsat 8 or 9, if scene is OLI or OLI_TIRS combined, value will reflect OLI quality score. If TIRS, the TIRS quality score will be used

Values:
9 = Best
0 = Worst
-1 = Image quality not calculated or assessed"""@en;
                                                                     rdfs:domain vas:Landsat-8_Product;
                                                                     rdfs:label "Image quality TIRS"@en;
                                                                     rdfs:range xsd:decimal;
                                                                     rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:landsat8ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#instrumentname> a owl:FunctionalProperty,
                                                                     owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                                   rdfs:comment """The instrument name used for acquiring the data.

Example: Multi-Spectral Instrument"""@en;
                                                                   rdfs:domain vas:Sentinel-2_Product;
                                                                   rdfs:label "Instrument name"@en;
                                                                   rdfs:range xsd:string;
                                                                   rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:sentinel2ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#landsatproductid> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                                     rdfs:comment """The naming convention of each L7 ETM+ Collection 1 Level-1 image is based on acquisition and processing parameters.

Format:
LXSS_LLLL_PPPRRR_YYYYMMDD_yyyymmdd_CC_TX

L = Landsat
X = Sensor (E = Enhanced Thematic Mapper Plus)
SS = Satellite (07 = Landsat 7)
LLLL = Processing Correction Level (L1TP = precision and terrain, L1GT = systematic terrain, L1GS = systematic)
PPP = WRS Path
RRR = WRS Row
YYYYMMDD = Acquisition Date expressed in Year, Month, Day
yyyymmdd = Processing Date expressed in Year, Month, Day
CC = Collection Number (01)
TX = Collection Category (RT = Real Time, T1 = Tier 1, T2 = Tier 2)

Example: LE07_L1TP_029030_20140715_20140805_02_T1"""@en;
                                                                     rdfs:domain vas:Landsat-8_Product;
                                                                     rdfs:label "Landsat product ID"@en;
                                                                     rdfs:range xsd:string;
                                                                     rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:landsat8ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#link> a owl:FunctionalProperty,
                                                           owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                         rdfs:comment """Download link for the product from https://scihub.copernicus.eu

Example: https://scihub.copernicus.eu/dhus/odata/v1/Products('95bec4b4-a2d4-4b6f-a7cd-1de5cb3e85b7')/$value"""@en;
                                                         rdfs:domain vas:Sentinel-2_Product;
                                                         rdfs:label "Product download link"@en;
                                                         rdfs:range xsd:anyURI;
                                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:sentinel2ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#link_alternative> a owl:FunctionalProperty,
                                                                       owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                                     rdfs:comment """Link to the product from https://scihub.copernicus.eu

Example: https://scihub.copernicus.eu/dhus/odata/v1/Products('95bec4b4-a2d4-4b6f-a7cd-1de5cb3e85b7')/"""@en;
                                                                     rdfs:domain vas:Sentinel-2_Product;
                                                                     rdfs:label "Link to product"@en;
                                                                     rdfs:range xsd:anyURI;
                                                                     rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:sentinel2ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#mapprojection> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                                  rdfs:comment """L0Ra map projection selectively applied to HDTs based on geographic location. Used for processed archive data.

Values:
HOM = Hotine Oblique Mercator
UTM = Universal Transverse Mercator"""@en;
                                                                  rdfs:domain vas:Landsat-8_Product;
                                                                  rdfs:label "Map projection"@en;
                                                                  rdfs:range xsd:string;
                                                                  rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:landsat8ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#orbitdirection> a owl:FunctionalProperty,
                                                                     owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                                   rdfs:comment """Orbit direccion while taking he product

Can be either 'ASCENDING' or 'DESCENDING'

Example: 'ASCENDING'"""@en;
                                                                   rdfs:domain vas:Sentinel-2_Product;
                                                                   rdfs:label "Orbit direction"@en;
                                                                   rdfs:range xsd:string;
                                                                   rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:sentinel2ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#orientation> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                                rdfs:comment """Orientation used in creating the image.

Values:
NOMINAL = Nominal Path
NORTH_UP = North Up
TRUE_NORTH = True North
USER = User"""@en;
                                                                rdfs:domain vas:Landsat-8_Product;
                                                                rdfs:label "Orientation"@en;
                                                                rdfs:range xsd:string;
                                                                rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:landsat8ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#origin> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                           rdfs:comment """Origin of the image

Values:
Example: \"Image courtesy of the U.S. Geological Survey\""""@en;
                                                           rdfs:domain vas:Landsat-8_Product;
                                                           rdfs:label "Origin"@en;
                                                           rdfs:range xsd:string;
                                                           rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:landsat8ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#platformname> a owl:FunctionalProperty,
                                                                   owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                                 rdfs:comment """The mission full name of the platform. This name is not a perfect identifier.

Example:Sentinel-2"""@en;
                                                                 rdfs:domain vas:Sentinel-2_Product;
                                                                 rdfs:label "Platform name"@en;
                                                                 rdfs:range xsd:string;
                                                                 rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:sentinel2ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#platformserialidentifier> a owl:FunctionalProperty,
                                                                               owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                                             rdfs:comment """The platform serial identifier is the sequence number of the platform among the mission

Example: Sentinel-2A"""@en;
                                                                             rdfs:domain vas:Sentinel-2_Product;
                                                                             rdfs:label "Platform serial identifier"@en;
                                                                             rdfs:range xsd:string;
                                                                             rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:sentinel2ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#processinglevel> a owl:FunctionalProperty,
                                                                      owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                                    rdfs:comment """The level of the last processing

Example: Level-2A"""@en;
                                                                    rdfs:domain vas:Sentinel-2_Product;
                                                                    rdfs:label "Processing level"@en;
                                                                    rdfs:range xsd:string;
                                                                    rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:sentinel2ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#size> a owl:FunctionalProperty,
                                                           owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                         rdfs:comment """Size of the product

Example: 634.50 MB"""@en;
                                                         rdfs:domain vas:Sentinel-2_Product;
                                                         rdfs:label "Size"@en;
                                                         rdfs:range xsd:string;
                                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:sentinel2ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#snowicepercentage> a owl:FunctionalProperty,
                                                                        owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                                      rdfs:comment """Percentage of snow ice

Example: 0.00018899999999999999"""@en;
                                                                      rdfs:domain vas:Sentinel-2_Product;
                                                                      rdfs:label "Snow ice percentage"@en;
                                                                      rdfs:range xsd:decimal;
                                                                      rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:sentinel2ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#title> a owl:FunctionalProperty,
                                                            owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                          rdfs:comment """Title

Example: S2A_MSIL2A_20170628T105651_N0205_R094_T30SUF_20170628T110445"""@en;
                                                          rdfs:domain vas:Sentinel-2_Product;
                                                          rdfs:label "Title"@en;
                                                          rdfs:range xsd:string;
                                                          rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:sentinel2ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#utmzone> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                            rdfs:comment """UTM (Universal Transverse Mercator) zone number in a map projection. A negative zone indicates that the false northing needs to be applied to the northing coordinate and a positive zone indicates that the false northing has been applied.

Values:
Negative Zone = Indicates that the false northing needs to be applied.
Positive Zone = Indicates that the false northing has been applied."""@en;
                                                            rdfs:domain vas:Landsat-8_Product;
                                                            rdfs:label "UTM zone"@en;
                                                            rdfs:range xsd:string;
                                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:landsat8ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#vegetationpercentage> a owl:FunctionalProperty,
                                                                           owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                                         rdfs:comment """Percentage of vegetation

Example: 10.589334000000001"""@en;
                                                                         rdfs:domain vas:Sentinel-2_Product;
                                                                         rdfs:label "Vegetation percentage"@en;
                                                                         rdfs:range xsd:decimal;
                                                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:sentinel2ProductProperties.
<http://khaos.uma.es/green-senti/earth-observation#waterpercentage> a owl:FunctionalProperty,
                                                                      owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                                                    rdfs:comment """Water of percentage

Example: 15.87375"""@en;
                                                                    rdfs:domain vas:Sentinel-2_Product;
                                                                    rdfs:label "Water percentage"@en;
                                                                    rdfs:range xsd:decimal;
                                                                    rdfs:subPropertyOf vas:sentinel2ProductProperties.
aws:WindVane a owl:Class;
